  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A 3D Deburr `width` is now the chamfer chord `w = 2 s sin(theta / 2)` across each edge. `theta` is the wedge angle of the edge. The setback `s` and the tip drop `s / tan(half-angle)` come from the wedge of each edge. `Chamfer2D.width` does not change.\n- New `finishing3d::DeburrBreak` (in the new `deburr_size.rs`). `DeburrParams` and `OpParams::Deburr` each get one field, `sizing`, which holds:\n  - `mode`: `ConstantWidth` (default) or `ConstantDepth` (`s = d / cos(theta / 2)`).\n  - `depth`: the depth that Constant Depth holds on each edge.\n  - `profile`: `Chamfer` (default) or `Round`.\n  - `passes`: 1 to 100.\n- Passes go from the outer pass to the final pass. Pass `k` of `n` cuts the setback `s * k / n`. Only the final break is declared as an `EdgeBreak`, and each pass stays above it.\n- A Round profile refuses by name: \"a Round break profile needs a ball-tipped cutter, and the chamfer mill is a sharp cone\".\n- Runs chain only edges that have the same drop. Thus each run keeps one depth and one declared break.\n- Range limits: Constant Width sizes wedges from 30 degrees up. Constant Depth sizes wedges up to 150 degrees. The ride skips an edge outside the range, and a note gives the count.\n- The project file goes from v74 to v75. A v74 Deburr `width` is multiplied by `sqrt(2)` at load. On a 90-degree edge the cut depth stays the same. The new keys are `break_mode`, `break_depth`, `break_profile` and `passes`. They are always written, and an absent key reads as one Constant Width chamfer pass. MCP gets the keys from `ParamsDto`.\n- The record bound (`stock_sim_breaks::declared_width`) and the flute-length door now use the largest setback of the size law (`DeburrBreak::max_setback`).\n- UI: the Deburr Geometry tab has new rows: Break mode, Break width or Break depth, Break profile, and Number of passes.\n- The cache stamp digests the sizing only when it is not the default.\n\nNote for the maintainer: the issue text says v61 to v62. Main was at v74, so this PR uses v74 to v75. The meaning of `width` changes for new operations and for MCP clients: the same number now cuts a smaller break (by `sqrt(2)` on a 90-degree edge). Project files are migrated. Decide if the title needs `!`. The decisions are in `docs/decisions/1890-deburr-chord-width.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nBefore this PR, `width` was the radius of the cone at the edge's level. That is the setback on a horizontal face, not the chamfer width on the edge. There was no depth mode and no multi-pass mode.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pins:\n- `crates/motion/tests/deburr_sizing.rs`:\n  - `constant_width_holds_the_chord_on_a_120_and_a_90_degree_wedge`\n  - `constant_depth_holds_the_depth_on_a_120_and_a_90_degree_wedge`\n  - `passes_step_from_the_outer_break_to_the_final_one_inside_the_declared_break` (each cutting tip is on or above `EdgeBreak::floor_at`)\n  - `a_round_profile_on_a_sharp_cone_refuses_by_name`\n  - `the_size_law_names_the_wedges_it_reaches_and_its_bound`\n- `crates/motion/tests/deburr.rs`: `deburr_at_the_wall_corner_is_chamfer_byte_for_byte` now passes `w = 2.0 * sqrt(2)`. On unchanged code it failed: the tip was at `-2.828427`, not `-2.0`.\n- `crates/app/tests/deburr_chord_width.rs`:\n  - `a_v74_deburr_width_steps_up_by_sqrt_2_and_a_current_file_does_not`\n  - `constant_depth_in_two_passes_generates_inside_its_declared_break`\n  - `a_round_profile_refuses_by_name_at_generate`\n  - `zero_passes_or_no_depth_is_refused_at_the_command`\n  - `the_sizing_edit_undoes_and_round_trips_in_the_file`\n  - `the_record_bound_is_the_largest_setback_of_the_size_law`\n  - `mcp_sets_the_break_mode_profile_and_passes`\n\nMutation checks (each mutation applied, pin red, then restored and green):\n- Setback law back to `s = width`: the congruence pin and 6 other `deburr.rs` tests are red.\n- Round refusal removed: `a_round_profile_on_a_sharp_cone_refuses_by_name` is red.\n- One pass only: `passes_step_...` is red.\n- v75 step removed from `apply.rs`: `a_v74_deburr_width_steps_up_...` is red.\n- `sizing.is_sane()` removed from `sane.rs`: `zero_passes_or_no_depth_is_refused_at_the_command` is red.\n- Bound back to `width`: `the_record_bound_is_the_largest_setback_of_the_size_law` is red.\n\nExpected-change updates to tests and fixtures:\n- The Deburr widths in existing tests are now the chord of the setback that each test used before (`x sqrt(2)`). The exception is `deburr_cache_stamp.rs`, which keeps `1.0` so that its legacy stamp constant stays valid. That also shows that the default sizing does not move a stamp.\n- `operations.rs::deburr_refuses_a_flank_too_short_for_the_break` now expects `19.3` mm (the conservative bound), not `7.1` mm.\n- `deburr_unreachable.rs` round-trip: the line of the absent key no longer needs the comma change.\n- `examples/catalog/2d/edge-work/build.camscript`: width `0.42426407`, which is the chord of the old 0.3 mm setback. The committed `.nc` is the same byte for byte.\n- `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj`: version 74 to 75 (it contains no Deburr).\n- UI placement test: the new Geometry rows are added.\n\nGate:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` did not finish. In this run sccache stopped responding while it compiled `solidcore` and `camcraft_motion` (40 minutes with no rustc process). Thus I ran the same set of steps directly with cargo, without the wrapper:\n  - all `camcraft-app` test binaries: green after the expected-change updates (620+ results, 0 failed)\n  - motion `--lib` plus `deburr`, `deburr_filters`, `deburr_sizing`, `deburr_unreachable`, `finish3d`: green\n  - `camcraft-ui --lib`: 1383 passed\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `*.nc` or `*.cl` golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The ui integration suites (`crates/ui/tests/`) other than the lib tests.\n- The motion suites that the gate map selects and that do not touch deburr (for example `multiaxis`, `flow`, `pivot5d`).\n- A curved part with many wedge angles. Such a part gives more runs, because runs split at each new depth.\n- `examples/catalog/2d/edge-work/edge-work.camproj` stays at v73 and steps up on load. Its cached Deburr path becomes stale one time, because the stamp digests the new width.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs touch the same files but not the Deburr arms:\n- #3151, #3103, #3058, #2890, #2831, #2714, #2920, #2836 (operation params, sane, DTO).\n- #2920, #2836 and #2714 also change `PROJECT_VERSION` in `project/file.rs`. The PR that merges second must take the next version number.\n- #3142, #3115, #3108, #3059 and #2822 touch other arms of `generate.rs`.\n\nThe PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: 3D Deburr: `width` is now the chamfer width across the edge on each wedge angle (older projects are converted by sqrt(2)); new Constant Depth mode, multi-pass breaks, and a Round profile that refuses by name on a chamfer mill.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1890\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
